    "import.md": [
      {
        "row": [
          "# nC Runtime Import: ",
          {
            "path": [
              "import_path"
            ]
          },
          "\n\n## 1. Purpose\n`",
          {
            "path": [
              "import_path"
            ]
          },
          "` is the registered runtime import surface for the `",
          {
            "path": [
              "family_key"
            ]
          },
          "` family. It exposes operational functions under explicit import, capability, policy, and diagnostic contracts.\n\n## 2. Canonical compact import\n```n\nuse ",
          {
            "path": [
              "compact_import"
            ]
          },
          ";\n```\n\n## 3. Aliases\n",
          {
            "path": [
              "aliases_text"
            ]
          },
          "\n\n## 4. Mode availability\nAllowed: `[@runtime]` examples and runtime-aware compiler analysis.\n\nDenied: ",
          {
            "path": [
              "mode_denied"
            ]
          },
          ".\n\n## 5. Exported functions\n| Function | Signature | Return | Capability | Policy | Errors | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n",
          {
            "path": [
              "export_lines"
            ]
          },
          "\n\n## 6. Type contracts\nFunction signatures are the active type contract surface for this import. Generic exports keep their declared generic marker in the function name.\n\n## 7. Ownership rules\nOwnership follows the declared argument and return contracts. Memory-bearing families additionally require origin, bounds, alias, or lifecycle policies when listed below.\n\n## 8. Nullability rules\nNullability is explicit through `Option`, nullable pointer contracts, or family-specific refinement policies. Silent null widening is not part of this import contract.\n\n## 9. Bounds rules\nBounds-sensitive operations are governed by the required capabilities and policies listed below. Out-of-range or invalid state must surface a official runtime diagnostic.\n\n## 10. Side effects\nSide effects are limited to the family purpose and guarded by the declared capabilities. IO, filesystem, process, network, security, and memory families require their listed policy gates.\n\n## 11. Capabilities\n",
          {
            "path": [
              "cap_lines"
            ]
          },
          "\n\n## 12. Policies\n",
          {
            "path": [
              "policy_lines"
            ]
          },
          "\n\n## 13. Errors\n",
          {
            "path": [
              "error_lines"
            ]
          },
          "\n\n## 14. Positive examples\n- `",
          {
            "path": [
              "docs_evidence",
              "example_positive"
            ]
          },
          "`\n\n## 15. Negative examples\nNegative missing-use behavior is verified by `crates/ncc-cli/tests/runtime_family_closure.rs` using the first exported symbol for each discovered family.\n\n## 16. Strict mode\n`ncc runtime check <file> --strict` accepts explicit runtime imports in `[@runtime]` and rejects runtime imports in forbidden modes.\n\n## 17. Runtime report shape\nThe generated report for this family is stored at `",
          {
            "path": [
              "docs_evidence",
              "report_json"
            ]
          },
          "` and `",
          {
            "path": [
              "docs_evidence",
              "report_md"
            ]
          },
          "`.\n\n## 18. Industrial conformance checklist\n- import identity checked\n- export signatures checked\n- capabilities checked\n- policies checked\n- example check passed\n- runtime JSON report generated\n- runtime Markdown report generated\n\n## 19. Known non-goals\nThis import does not make runtime calls available without `use`, does not bypass capability/policy checks, and does not cross into `[@machine]` or `primitive[@]`.\n\n## 20. Evidence\n- exports command: `",
          {
            "path": [
              "docs_evidence",
              "exports_command"
            ]
          },
          "`\n- check command: `",
          {
            "path": [
              "docs_evidence",
              "check_command"
            ]
          },
          "`\n- report command: `",
          {
            "path": [
              "docs_evidence",
              "report_command"
            ]
          },
          "`\n- evidence hash: `",
          {
            "path": [
              "docs_evidence",
              "evidence_hash"
            ]
          },
          "`\n"
        ]
      }
    ],
